Z||000001||kornholio||08-18-99||08:26 PM||||My auto 86 SE cannot light it up...actually it can.  I'm the fool that stepped on the pedal when in neutral and shifted into drive. <br>Thats the only way it can light it up, for me at least.  I have since stopped doing that because I've been told that it messes up the transmission.
Z||000002||lowCG||08-18-99||08:55 PM||||The biggest difference I could find was the 80 pound weight gain for the GT,along with the Lancia-rip-off bodywork.
Z||000003||Cooter||08-18-99||10:09 PM||||Why does everybody say the fastback weighs 80 pounds more than a coupe?? I swapped the tail clip from my gt parts car onto my SE by myself and did not notice any difference in weight between the two. The only thing that was heavier was the decklid, but most of that is the spoiler. Where do y'all get these weight figures from?
Z||000004||TOM||08-18-99||10:46 PM||||Its not the GT over the SE that there is the 80 pound increase. Its from the L4 to the V6.
